      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "LI T'iao-yüan 李調元 (T. 羹堂 or 秔塘, H. 雨村, 贊菴, 童山, 鶴洲, 卍齋, 蠢翁), Dec. 29, 1734–1803, Jan. 14, scholar, bibliophile, and official, was a native of Lo-chiang, Szechwan. His father, Li Hua-nan 李化楠 (T. 廷節, H. 石亭, 讓齋, 1713–1769), was the first student of his district to become a chin-shih (1742) during the Ch'ing period.",
